>> title: Refried Beans
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, pinto, mexican, side, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: frijoles refritos
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr
>> step.1: simmer 1 1/2 hr
>> step.2: fry 6 min
>> step.3: mash
>> step.4: fry 10 min

Simmer @dried pinto beans{1%lb}(450 g; soaked overnight) in @water{8%cups}(1.9 L) with @white onion{1/2%large}(halved), @garlic{4%cloves}, and @bay leaf{1} until completely soft, ~{1 1/2%hr}.

Fry @yellow onion{1%small}(finely chopped) in @lard{1/3%cup}(70 g; or bacon fat) in a wide #skillet{} for ~{6%min}.

Add @&(~2)beans{} to @&(~1)onion{} with a cup of their cooking liquid and mash with a #potato masher{}.

Fry @&(~1)beans{} over medium heat, stirring, until thick enough to hold a line, ~{10%min}, with @kosher salt{2 1/2%tsp} and @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}.
